><title>Entry #297 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-297" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-11T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-297</id><summary type="html">Notice (Other)</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027633514?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-11T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Minute entry from 2026-09-10 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/Crowder-v.-LinkedIn-Corporation/" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#minute-entry-477591812</id><summary type="html">Motion Hearing AND Order on Motion for Leave to File AND ~Util - Set Deadlines</summary><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #296 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-296" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-296</id><summary type="html"> DISCOVERY ORDER addressing  288  Discovery Letter Brief.The attached order addresses the parties' discovery letter brief. It orders as follows:Within two court days of this order, the plaintiffs must identify up to twenty-five privilege -log entries for in camera review. The plaintiffs choose the entries, but the selection should span the challenged categories. LinkedIn then must lodge them for in camera review and include the selected documents in unredacted form (with the produced  redacted versions for comparison where applicable and the corresponding privilege log entries). LinkedIn also must provide updated privilege logs.This resolves ECF No. 288.Signed by Judge Laurel Beeler on 9/10/2026.(lblc2, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 9/10/2026)</summary><link href="https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cand.390494/gov.uscourts.cand.390494.296.0.pdf" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #295 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-295" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-295</id><summary type="html">Certificate/Proof of Service</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027632994?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #294 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-294" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-294</id><summary type="html">Attachments to an Administrative Motion to File Under Seal</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027632964?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #293 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-293" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-293</id><summary type="html">Opposition/Response to Motion</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027632939?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #292 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-292" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-292</id><summary type="html"> DISCOVERY ORDER addressing  285  Discovery Letter Brief.The attached order addresses the parties' discovery letter brief. It orders as follows:1. The plaintiffs' motion to compel LinkedIn to run the generative-AI search string acro ss four custodians and produce responsive documents hitting on the search string is granted. The plaintiffs' separate request to reopen depositions based on any newly-produced documents hitting on the search string is denied without prejudice.2. The plaintiffs' motion to compel unredacted or less-redacted versions of the two documents clawed back by LinkedIn is denied without prejudice. The plaintiffs may renew their motion by submitting the documents to the court for in camera r eview, which LinkedIn does not oppose.3. The plaintiffs' motion to reopen Mr. Pradhan's deposition is granted. The plaintiffs may examine Mr. Pradhan for one hour, remotely, with examination limited to any non-privileged discussions he had with counsel regarding his testimony during breaks at his August 24, 2026, deposition.This resolves ECF No. 285.Signed by Judge Laurel Beeler on September 10, 2026.(lblc2, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 9/10/2026)</summary><link href="https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cand.390494/gov.uscourts.cand.390494.292.0.pdf" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #290 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-290" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-290</id><summary type="html">Certificate/Proof of Service</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027627181?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #289 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-289" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-289</id><summary type="html">Notice (Other)</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027627122?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #288 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-288" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</published><id>https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-288</id><summary type="html">Discovery Letter Brief</summary><link href="https://ecf.cand.uscourts.gov/doc1/035027627045?caseid=390494" length="0" rel="enclosure" /><updated>2026-09-10T00:00:00-07:00</updated></entry><entry><title>Entry #287 in Crowder v. LinkedIn Corporation, 4:22-cv-00237</title><link href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/62592046/crowder-v-linkedin-corporation/?order_by=desc#entry-287" rel="alternate" /><published>2026-09-10T00:00:00-